.TH WAIT_EXITSTATUS 3
.SH NAME
wait_exitstatus \- extract the exit code from a wait status
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "wait.h"
.PP
.BI "int wait_exitstatus(int " wstat ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wait_exitstatus
extracts the numeric exit code a child passed to
.BR exit (3)/_exit(2)
from
.IR wstat ,
a status previously filled in by
.BR wait_pid (3),
.BR wait_nointr (3),
.BR wait_nohang (3),
.BR wait_pid_nohang (3),
or the
.I *pids
variants. Portable across platforms:
.I wstat
is a packed status requiring this decoding on POSIX, but is already the
plain exit code on WINDOWS_NATIVE (GetExitCodeProcess()) -- callers should
always use this instead of the POSIX
.B WEXITSTATUS()
macro to stay portable.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The exit code, valid only if
.BR wait_ifexited (3)
returned nonzero for the same
.IR wstat .
.SH SEE ALSO
wait_ifexited(3), wait_pid(3)
